  "body": "## What\n\nAdd two wire EDM cases in `examples/catalog/edm/`.\n- Case 1: Wire Contour cuts a vertical profile from a DXF and posts.\n- Case 2: a tapered Wire Contour that the machine refuses.\n\n## Notes\n\nMachine: `assets/machines/sodick-alc400g.mch`. Its description says that the post refuses each taper (#1800). `crates/app/tests/mcp_wire_contour.rs` shows the refusal. Case 2 needs the #2392 sub-issue \"a case can expect a refusal\". Case 1 does not.\n\nDone means: The case folder obeys `examples/catalog/README.md`: `model/` with its generator script, `build.camscript`, `<case>.camproj`, `<case>.nc` and `README.md`. The geometry is original (Clean-Room Protocol). `cargo xtask catalog --check` and `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog` pass. The README says what the case shows and what to look at. Case 1 posts. Case 2 compares its `refusal.txt`.\n\nFile each refusal or wrong output that the work finds as its own bug. Link the bug on #2392. A missing parameter in an MCP tool is a new `area:mcp` issue.\n\nPart of #2392\n",
